  "DV-C1-RES-TR-MAP": {
    sources: ["DfE Key stage 4 performance: subject points by school (GCSE (9-1) Full Course entries, DfE 9-1 points table; GCSE Double Award scored from its grades as two entries), via VicData's subject rollup, 2021/22 to {year} (GCSE page)", "DfE A level and other 16 to 18 results: average points per entry by school, subject and exact qualification (DfE points table, size-weighted), 2021/22 to {year} (Post-16 page)", "DfE grade counts by school, subject and qualification (KS4 subject entries / KS5 subject results, modern and historic files), 2021/22 to {year}", "The comparison set: by default VicData's '10 nearest schools' (school locations, sector, phase and gender from VicData's schools table, GIAS; schools with pupils of this age from the DfE school census), or a saved set or a chosen list", "School locations (easting and northing) from VicData's schools table"],
    geography: "The school and each school in the comparison set chosen in Comparisons, on a map.",
    years: "From 2022/23 (or a later 'From' year) to the latest year held.",
    leftOut: ["At GCSE, an independent school whose latest published English and maths grade 4+ figure is 0% while its Attainment 8 is above 5 is treated as sitting IGCSEs (which DfE's tables don't count) and is left out of every GCSE comparison and ranking: national, regional, LA and set. A '10 nearest' set fills to 10 with the next nearest eligible schools, and a line says how many nearer schools aren't ranked and how far the ten reach; a saved or chosen list is not refilled, and a note names the schools left out. The school itself is kept, but its whole-school headline history is withheld.", "Schools with no recorded location are not plotted.", "A school with no figure for your subject is a hollow grey dot.", "A grade rate is worked out only on the scale it belongs to: Grade 4+ on GCSE 9-1 and Double Award pairs (both digits 4 or above); A*–E on the A-level scale at Post-16. Vocational, IB, T Level and Pre-U rows get no figure.", "Non-grades (Suppressed, No result, X, Covid impacted, COVID result, Supp, Not Awarded) are left out of both sides of every grade share.", "No small-entries rule is applied on this map."],
    steps: ["For each school in the set we take its result in your subject: average points (GCSE: GCSE (9-1) Full Course; Post-16: the same exact qualification), or a grade rate scored from that school's own grade counts for the same subject and qualification, in the same way as your school's.", "For each school we work out the change from its first figure from 2022/23 on to its latest, in points or percentage points.", "Each dot is coloured by that change on one scale centred on zero: green for the biggest rise in the set, red for the biggest fall, pale amber for little change.", "Dot size is the school's entries in the subject in the last year (graded entries on a grade rate).", "Your school wears a thick ring."],
    rounding: ["Changes in points to 1 decimal place; in whole percentage points on rates."],
  },
