    steps: ["Each school's figure is: with a subject in focus, its entries in the subject (Candidates) or its result in the subject — average points (GCSE: GCSE (9-1) Full Course points; Post-16: the same exact qualification), or a grade rate scored from that school's own grade counts for the same subject and qualification; with no subject, Attainment 8 (GCSE) or A-level average points per entry (Post-16), or the number of pupils at the end of Key stage 4 / 16 to 18 students.", "Schools are ranked on the latest year, highest first; schools with the same figure share a place and the next place is skipped.", "Each row shows the place, the school, its sector, its figure and its distance from your school.", "On a subject ranking across a whole population, the rows are a window at real places: the top, the schools around yours and the bottom."],
